    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["SOLID principles were designed for object-oriented systems under significant change pressure. Applied indiscriminately, they produce over-engineered systems where simple logic is buried under layers of interfaces and abstractions. A function that formats a date does not need to depend on a ", _jsx(_components.code, {
