    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "The symptom of over-applied SOLID is a codebase where it is difficult to trace a single user action from entry point to database because the logic is distributed across dozens of small, single-responsibility classes connected by interfaces. Understanding the system requires holding the entire dependency graph in your head. In small teams or early-stage systems, this overhead can significantly impede velocity without providing proportionate benefit."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h3, {
