    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "As noted in the DRY section, not all code that looks the same represents the same knowledge. Aggressively eliminating all apparent duplication leads to premature abstractions that couple unrelated concerns. When two modules happen to share some logic today but evolve independently, merging them creates a forcing function: future changes to one must also consider the impact on the other. The coupling tax compounds over time."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
