    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "The principles and patterns covered in this article have lasted decades precisely because they address problems that recur wherever software is built under change pressure. DRY prevents the divergence that comes from encoding the same knowledge in multiple places. YAGNI prevents the overhead of complexity that earns no current return. SOLID provides a framework for managing coupling and responsibility in object-oriented systems. Design patterns provide a shared vocabulary for structural solutions to recurring problems."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
